WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.380
ai just helped students jump almost a full grade on a marketing project, but it raises a big question about what they actually learned. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 152. Researchers studied over 1000 students and discovered that access to GPT 4.0 lifted scores on a real marketing assignment by nearly a full point on the usual 5 point scale. That jump turns a solid B into something closer to an A-on paper.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:57.880
Think of the AI like an extremely fast research assistant who can sort ideas, write smooth paragraphs, and fix awkward phrasing in seconds. The same skills that earned top marks in school, clear structure, polished wording, and quick organization, happened to be the exact things these tools already do well. Yet the study never checked whether the students understood the marketing ideas any better afterward. It only measured the final paper that teachers saw.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:20.640
For anyone still in class, that difference matters because the output can look stronger while the actual learning stays the same. Schools may soon need new ways to test real understanding, such as spoken explanations or writing done right in the room. On the helpful side, the same tool can act like a personal tutor that helped you organize thoughts before you start writing on your own.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:33.620
You can test the same effect yourself right now by opening chat GPT on your phone, writing one paragraph of an assignment alone, then asking the AI to rewrite it and comparing the two versions side by side.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:50.780
The researchers worked with 1,053 students at a university, a large enough group that the pattern deserves attention. The biggest improvements showed up in organizing information and producing clean paragraphs. The parts current AI models have practiced on millions of examples.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:59.260
Picture the AI as a very fast auto complete that has read thousands of high scoring school papers and learned what that style looks like.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:12.600
It breaks your request into tiny pieces called tokens, each roughly one word or part of a word. Then it uses patterns from everything it has seen before to guess which token should come next, one small step at a time.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.300
Over thousands of those tiny guesses, a full answer appears that follows the shape of work teachers usually reward.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:27.180
It is like watching your phone finish a text message except the prediction stretches across an entire essay instead of one sentence.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:35.940
The model does not carry the deep knowledge a student builds by studying the topic itself. It only knows what successful answers tend to sound like.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:48.440
That gap explains why grades rose even though long-term understanding was not measured. The process feels less mysterious once you see it as rapid pattern-based prediction rather than true comprehension.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:55.620
Watching the steps unfold makes the grade boost feel like a very skilled auto complete that has read a lot of textbooks.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:05.720
The result is impressive on the page, yet it still leaves the real thinking up to you. Now for two simple experiments you can run today with tools already on your phone.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:12.260
Chat GPT can turn any photo into a split page layout that looks like a page from a photography journal.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:21.300
One half shows your original picture and the other half shows a hand drawn ink sketch of the same scene, complete with paper texture and nice lettering.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.400
It keeps the people, poses, and mood from your shot while adding that editorial feel.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:33.580
Open the chat GPT app, start a new chat, upload a photo from your camera roll, and paste this prompt.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:39.080
Create a nostalgic editorial photo to sketch artbook page based on the reference image.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.640
Divide the page vertically into two connected sections. Send it and see the layout appear.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:50.720
You can reply with small changes like make the sketch line softer if the first version is not quite right.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.760
The feature works on the free version so anyone can try it immediately.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.620
It turns ordinary snapshots into something that feels like a page from a travel diary or artbook.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:05.420
The second quick change takes less than a minute and makes chats feel more personal.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.980
On the chat GPT website or app, click your profile picture in the bottom left corner.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:15.360
Go to profile and type whatever name you want to appear in conversations.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.600
The update shows up instantly across every chat and stays until you change it again.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:26.460
It is useful if you share a device with family or simply want a fun nickname instead of your real name.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.180
No extra apps or settings beyond the normal menu are needed.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:38.960
In other quick updates, AI coding assistants often overestimate how long a task will take, sometimes by 10 times the real time.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:43.660
They also write their own work about 20 points higher than human reviewers do.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:49.240
The gap appears most clearly on longer projects that require planning several steps ahead.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:58.740
Separately, Virginia Beach Schools signed an agreement to bring chat GPT tools into classrooms as part of testing how AI can support everyday lessons.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:03.760
The partnership joins a growing list of districts exploring direct classroom use.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.720
Parents and students will now see what that looks like in their own schools.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:13.640
That's it for today. Remember, every AI expert started exactly where you are right now.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:17.680
If something we talked about today made you curious, go try it.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:23.420
That's literally how learning works. Stay curious, keep experimenting and we'll see you tomorrow.

